# D51 / `todo/t0718` — `unify`'s smart-pointer coercion is keyed on the TYPED
# builtin IDENTITY (`DefInfo.builtin_kind`), never on the definition's NAME.
#
# ⛔ THE AXES DISAGREE, AND THIS ROW IS THE PROOF. `Weak` and `Mutex` are BOTH
# `DerefWrapperKind::NonDerefContainer` on the field-access axis — and only
# `Mutex` is transparent for coercion. So the coercion axis CANNOT be derived
# from the field-access one: writing
# `is_coercion_transparent = deref_wrapper_kind() == Some(NonDerefContainer)`
# turns this row green and makes `Weak[int]` unify with `int`.
#
# Measured AT THE ARM, not read off the source: `Weak[int]` has one type
# argument, so it DOES reach the guard, and the guard answers `false`. That is
# why the identity carries one variant per NAME, never per axis class.
# Asserted by `coercion_identity_weak_is_not_coercion_transparent`.

void take_w(Weak[int] w):
    print(1)

void main():
    print(take_w(5))
